WEBVTT

00:00:58.500 --> 00:00:59.820
He's in my class at school.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:02.140
This is Dave Bray, my brother-in-law.

00:01:02.950 --> 00:01:04.670
I'm sorry, Relay, for our appointment, Dave.

00:01:05.070 --> 00:01:06.480
Oh, well. How can I help you?

00:01:06.640 --> 00:01:07.400
Well, I...

00:01:10.180 --> 00:01:10.580
Yes.

00:01:11.490 --> 00:01:14.910
I've been trying to figure out what to do when I graduate from high school.

00:01:15.620 --> 00:01:17.890
Well, most of the kids have the same problem.

00:01:18.070 --> 00:01:19.150
We all want to get jobs.

00:01:19.310 --> 00:01:21.590
I know I want to work, at least until I'm married.

00:01:22.150 --> 00:01:24.770
And I know I have to work, even after I'm...

00:01:25.650 --> 00:01:27.680
I know, I have the same problem myself.

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:29.700
I guess everybody gets the willies.

00:01:29.800 --> 00:01:29.960
We're...

00:01:30.060 --> 00:01:31.740
about what to do when he gets out of high school.

00:01:31.920 --> 00:01:35.280
Well, I know Pat is kind of interested in working here,

00:01:35.460 --> 00:01:38.320
and frankly, I've never thought about working in a bank.

00:01:38.970 --> 00:01:42.210
Well, neither did I until I began looking around.

00:01:43.440 --> 00:01:44.960
When I graduated from high school,

00:01:45.180 --> 00:01:48.400
I knew I wasn't going to college, I couldn't afford to.

00:01:49.740 --> 00:01:51.640
So I wanted to find something with a future.

00:01:52.660 --> 00:01:55.910
I wanted something good, solid, and secure.

00:01:57.000 --> 00:01:58.680
Something, something I could grow with.

00:01:58.880 --> 00:01:59.440
What do you mean?

00:02:00.480 --> 00:02:05.470
Well, as long as there's money, they have banks to handle and service it.

00:02:06.650 --> 00:02:09.460
I figure both are going to be around for a long time.

00:02:09.740 --> 00:02:12.720
So I figured that a bank was a good permanent place to work.

00:02:12.980 --> 00:02:14.200
I would think so.

00:02:14.580 --> 00:02:16.960
And banking isn't just a job, it's a career.

00:02:17.370 --> 00:02:18.750
I hadn't thought of it that way.

00:02:19.490 --> 00:02:27.500
And besides being a secure, comfortable place to work, you, I don't know, you feel good working in a bank.

00:02:27.870 --> 00:02:28.670
And why shouldn't you?

00:02:31.340 --> 00:02:35.400
The people you work with are friendly and happy because they share a common interest.

00:02:35.580 --> 00:02:44.010
They're doing a job that's well-respected in the community in which they live,

00:02:44.550 --> 00:02:45.890
in the whole country for that matter.

00:02:49.860 --> 00:02:52.520
They've got good jobs and plenty of chance to get ahead.

00:02:53.000 --> 00:02:54.530
They know it, and they like it.

00:02:55.340 --> 00:02:57.900
It's kind of stimulating to work in an atmosphere like that.

00:02:58.750 --> 00:02:59.970
And you like working in a...

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:06.760
bank because banks help millions of people save for a better future. You know, large or small,

00:03:07.360 --> 00:03:12.920
every man's bank account is a personal and important thing to that man. It's nice to be

00:03:12.920 --> 00:03:19.680
trusted with it. Banks lend people the money to buy that house they've been dreaming about.

00:03:20.420 --> 00:03:26.800
Also lend farmers and people in industries the money they need. In time of war, banks lend

00:03:26.800 --> 00:03:29.960
millions, in fact billions of dollars, to help finance.

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:33.660
that make the materials we need in order to defend ourselves.

00:03:36.360 --> 00:03:39.980
Big and little. Banks serve and help everybody.

00:03:41.750 --> 00:03:43.850
That's all wonderfully interesting, Dave.

00:03:44.110 --> 00:03:47.030
But I still don't see what jobs there are in banks,

00:03:47.330 --> 00:03:49.110
for me or Jim or anybody.

00:03:49.700 --> 00:03:51.820
I'll tell you what I'm gonna do.

00:03:56.180 --> 00:03:59.140
Let's take a look over there.

00:04:01.660 --> 00:04:08.880
Judy Parrish. She's a teller now but she hasn't always been one. She came to work

00:04:08.880 --> 00:04:12.680
for the bank right after she graduated from high school. Started by doing

00:04:12.680 --> 00:04:19.400
clerical and messenger work. She was given a simple job of arranging checks in

00:04:19.400 --> 00:04:26.280
alphabetical order. She learned the importance of accuracy by running the

00:04:26.280 --> 00:04:29.720
proof machine that sorts and adds checks all in one operation.

00:04:32.590 --> 00:04:34.550
Soon, Judy moved into the bookkeeping department.

00:04:35.160 --> 00:04:37.800
At first, she did simple but important jobs,

00:04:37.820 --> 00:04:39.620
such as adding short lists of checks.

00:04:43.660 --> 00:04:46.040
She was assigned to the posting and filing of checks

00:04:46.040 --> 00:04:47.140
for individual customers.

00:04:48.170 --> 00:04:49.970
She quickly learned the customer's signatures.

00:04:50.650 --> 00:04:52.510
She'd know a forgery if she ever saw one.

00:04:55.470 --> 00:04:56.770
She began to see what was behind

00:04:56.770 --> 00:04:58.230
all the steps she was handling,

00:04:58.350 --> 00:04:59.960
and she was getting a good-

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:06.320
fundamental knowledge of the banking business so by now she was ready to

00:05:06.320 --> 00:05:12.670
advance into a teller's job been a kind of natural growth into this job for Judy

00:05:12.670 --> 00:05:18.300
she learned to recognize signatures and names and now the names and signatures

00:05:18.300 --> 00:05:23.950
are alive she's meeting people and helping them personally each job has

00:05:23.950 --> 00:05:29.060
taught her a little something about the next one so you see everything you do

00:05:29.060 --> 00:05:29.860
helps you to learn

00:05:31.240 --> 00:05:34.060
and everything you learn helps you to move ahead

00:05:34.060 --> 00:05:35.080
in your banking career.

00:05:35.640 --> 00:05:37.240
You grow and learn as you work.

00:05:37.540 --> 00:05:41.120
Yes, one job sort of leads into the next one.

00:05:41.300 --> 00:05:44.210
That's right, you're always in training for the job ahead.

00:05:45.260 --> 00:05:46.780
That's why banks promote from within

00:05:46.780 --> 00:05:48.420
their own groups of employees.

00:05:49.490 --> 00:05:53.320
Take me for instance, when I came from high school,

00:05:53.540 --> 00:05:55.510
I was a messenger for a while like Judy.

00:05:56.460 --> 00:05:58.860
Worked through several jobs and got to be a teller

00:05:58.860 --> 00:05:59.920
quicker than I thought I would.

00:06:02.750 --> 00:06:08.700
also handled the job of general bookkeeper for a while gave me a wonderful bird's eye view of

00:06:08.700 --> 00:06:16.740
everything that goes on in a bank then i was back on the human side of banking opening new accounts

00:06:17.110 --> 00:06:24.510
meeting the people who were beginning to build for their future and when i was promoted to my

00:06:24.510 --> 00:06:26.930
In my present job, I got an officer's title.

00:06:27.130 --> 00:06:29.960
Now I...

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:33.120
I spend a lot of my time interviewing borrowers, making loans.

00:06:33.420 --> 00:06:37.750
But of course, all this didn't happen overnight.

00:06:38.460 --> 00:06:40.560
You have to plan, and you have to work.

00:06:43.680 --> 00:06:46.000
It takes time to grow and learn.

00:06:46.200 --> 00:06:46.980
Well, I can see.

00:06:47.750 --> 00:06:49.310
But, gee, how do you get started?

00:06:49.580 --> 00:06:51.580
What do you have to know to get a job in the bank?

00:06:52.410 --> 00:06:54.850
Well, banks don't hire just anybody, Jim.

00:06:58.800 --> 00:06:59.340
But, uh...

00:07:00.350 --> 00:07:03.040
If you're honest, have a high school education.

00:07:03.380 --> 00:07:05.410
Did pretty well in arithmetic.

00:07:05.590 --> 00:07:06.770
Hey, I'm pretty good at figures.

00:07:06.970 --> 00:07:08.550
Well, there's a lot of figuring in a bank.

00:07:11.930 --> 00:07:15.640
Oh, and there's a lot of contact with people, too, working in a bank.

00:07:16.290 --> 00:07:17.650
So you should like people.

00:07:18.470 --> 00:07:20.130
Not only that, they should like you.

00:07:20.310 --> 00:07:21.070
Well, sure.

00:07:22.460 --> 00:07:23.380
Let's put it this way.

00:07:24.600 --> 00:07:29.820
Working in a bank appeals to people who like a dignified, secure job with good pay.

00:07:30.700 --> 00:07:32.980
At a place that has a lot of prestige in the community.

00:07:33.960 --> 00:07:38.810
Of course, it would be nice if everybody could have a college education,

00:07:38.810 --> 00:07:41.080
but even if you haven't got one,

00:07:41.220 --> 00:07:43.760
you can help yourself get ahead by studying banking.

00:07:44.130 --> 00:07:44.630
What do you mean?

00:07:46.490 --> 00:07:48.150
The American Institute of Banking.

00:07:48.380 --> 00:07:48.960
What's that?

00:07:49.220 --> 00:07:51.740
It's an educational service within the banking system

00:07:51.740 --> 00:07:55.460
to help bank employees grow and learn while they work.

00:07:58.380 --> 00:07:59.960
American Institute of Banking...

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:05.010
courses teach you the fundamentals of banking, give you a good solid basis for moving up the

00:08:05.010 --> 00:08:10.250
banking ladder, right from the start. In several hundred cities or towns in the country, there

00:08:10.250 --> 00:08:18.970
are chapters or local schools. When I was in the service, I kept taking AIB correspondence courses,

00:08:19.330 --> 00:08:25.440
so when I got out of the army, I not only came back to a job with a good future, I came back a

00:08:25.440 --> 00:08:29.970
little ahead of the game. Well, there's one thing certain, it isn't hard to sell the bank.

00:08:30.160 --> 00:08:32.020
Everybody likes money.

00:08:32.540 --> 00:08:35.260
Sure, but banks don't really sell money.

00:08:36.030 --> 00:08:38.210
The thing banks have to sell is services.

00:08:39.040 --> 00:08:42.340
Your knowledge, your ability, your honesty

00:08:42.340 --> 00:08:44.200
and taking care of people's money.

00:08:44.770 --> 00:08:47.250
You know, all of a sudden I'm kind of interested.

00:08:48.000 --> 00:08:49.700
Banking's good to be interested in.

00:08:52.300 --> 00:08:54.440
Banking isn't a flash in the pan.

00:08:55.240 --> 00:08:57.000
It's a solid lifetime career.

00:08:57.730 --> 00:08:59.970
The opportunities to advance, to...

00:09:00.060 --> 00:09:03.040
move up are as good as you want to make for yourself.

00:09:03.840 --> 00:09:07.370
And well, if you work hard, do your best,

00:09:08.570 --> 00:09:11.570
you'll find as much true happiness and as much real security

00:09:11.570 --> 00:09:14.090
in banking as you will in any other business in the world.

00:09:15.640 --> 00:09:17.600
I don't know what could be better than that.

00:09:18.350 --> 00:09:19.750
But what about people like me?

00:09:20.420 --> 00:09:21.960
I'm not going to work all my life.

00:09:22.380 --> 00:09:24.820
Well, even if you just work in a bank for a while, Pat,

00:09:25.130 --> 00:09:28.550
the things you learn about checks, about money, about people,

00:09:28.890 --> 00:09:29.970
those things stay with you.

00:09:30.250 --> 00:09:31.470
And we'll help you later on.

00:09:32.620 --> 00:09:32.940
Hmm.

00:09:34.960 --> 00:09:35.320
Yes.

00:09:38.130 --> 00:09:40.710
Well, if you two men will excuse me, I've gotten shot.
